1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,650
A robot flew into space to rescue a telescope.
一台机器人飞上太空去救一台望远镜，

2
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:05,180
Then the robot started spinning out of control.
结果它自己先转晕了。

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:05,980
Now NASA says:
现在NASA宣布：

4
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:07,740
the telescope can't be saved.
望远镜救不回来了。

5
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:09,470
This was a real space rescue,
这是一次真实的太空救援，

6
00:00:09,470 --> 00:00:10,720
and a real failure.
也是一次真实的失败。

7
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,630
It's called Swift.
它叫Swift，

8
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:14,140
It worked in space for almost twenty two years.
在太空里干了将近22年。

9
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:15,650
It was built to last two years,
原本只设计用两年，

10
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:18,400
and it caught more than two thousand gamma ray bursts.
它抓到了两千多次伽马射线暴。

11
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,010
Gamma ray bursts are the biggest blasts in the universe,
伽马射线暴是宇宙里最猛的爆炸，

12
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:23,700
and Swift could swing around to look in about a minute.
Swift发现后，大约一分钟就能扭头去看。

13
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,970
Today's question: space is nearly empty,
今天的问题：太空几乎是空的，

14
00:00:25,970 --> 00:00:27,850
so why do satellites fall down?
卫星为什么还会掉下来？

15
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:28,640
First, a secret:
先说个秘密：

16
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:30,810
being in orbit means falling all the time.
在轨道上，本来就一直在往下掉。

17
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:34,360
It just flies sideways so fast, seven and a half kilometers a second,
只是它横着飞得太快，每秒七公里半，

18
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,850
that the ground keeps curving away beneath it.
地面一直弯下去，它永远掉不到。

19
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:38,610
Always falling, never landing.
一直在掉，一直落不了地，

20
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:39,670
That's an orbit.
这就叫轨道。

21
00:00:39,670 --> 00:00:41,040
Like throwing a ball so hard
就像把一个球扔得飞快，

22
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,270
that it falls all the way around the Earth.
它就绕着地球一直掉下去。

23
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:44,850
But a few hundred kilometers up,
可是几百公里高的地方，

24
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:46,490
there's still a whisper of air.
还剩一丁点空气。

25
00:00:46,490 --> 00:00:48,700
Slam into it at seven kilometers a second,
每秒七公里多迎面撞上去，

26
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,560
and that whisper becomes a brake.
这一丁点空气就成了刹车。

27
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,910
Twist one, the weird one:
反转一，最反直觉：

28
00:00:51,910 --> 00:00:54,030
the brake makes the satellite faster.
刹车反而让卫星变快了。

29
00:00:54,030 --> 00:00:56,600
Lose a little energy, and it drops a little lower.
被拖慢一点，它就掉低一点，

30
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,160
And lower orbits are faster.
而低轨道跑得更快。

31
00:00:58,160 --> 00:00:59,320
Lower means thicker air,
越掉越低，空气越来越密，

32
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:00,750
which means harder braking.
刹得越来越狠。

33
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:02,000
It's a snowball effect:
这像一个越滚越大的雪球，

34
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,640
the final months go fastest.
最后几个月掉得最快。

35
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:04,210
Twist two:
反转二：

36
00:01:04,210 --> 00:01:05,370
the Sun joined in.
太阳也来插了一脚。

37
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:07,760
When the Sun is active, it heats the upper air,
太阳活跃的年份，把高空大气晒得膨胀，

38
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:10,180
and the air puffs up to where satellites fly.
空气一直涨到卫星的高度。

39
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:12,510
Swift started about six hundred kilometers up.
Swift一开始在大约600公里高，

40
00:01:12,510 --> 00:01:16,080
By October twentieth, it was down to about two hundred seventy five.
10月20号只剩大约275公里。

41
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:17,520
And Swift has no thrusters.
它自己没有推进器，

42
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,350
It could only watch itself sink.
只能眼看着往下沉。

43
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:20,470
It needed outside help:
只能靠外援：

44
00:01:20,470 --> 00:01:21,860
someone to give it a push.
有人来推它一把。

45
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:24,080
So NASA paid about thirty million dollars
于是NASA花了大约3000万美元，

46
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:25,220
for a rescue robot.
请人造一个救援机器人。

47
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,560
The company is Katalyst. The ship is LINK.
公司叫Katalyst，飞船叫LINK，

48
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,560
It was built in about nine months.
大约九个月就造好了。

49
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:31,950
The plan: grab Swift with three robot arms,
计划：用三只机械臂抓住Swift，

50
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:33,190
and push it back up.
再把它推回高处。

51
00:01:33,190 --> 00:01:35,500
That's like reaching out to grab another car
这就像在每秒七公里多的车流里，

52
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,940
in traffic moving seven kilometers a second.
伸手去抓另一辆车。

53
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:39,420
It launched on July third.
7月3号发射，

54
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,710
Three weeks later, it began to tumble.
可三周后，它就开始乱转。

55
00:01:41,710 --> 00:01:42,370
Twist three:
反转三：

56
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:43,970
its own wheels let it down.
坑它的，是它自己的轮子。

57
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:45,990
In space, there's no wall to push on.
太空里转身没有墙可以扶，

58
00:01:45,990 --> 00:01:48,180
Spacecraft turn using reaction wheels.
靠的是飞船里的反作用轮。

59
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:50,680
Sit on an office chair, spin a wheel one way,
坐在转椅上，把手里的轮子往一边转，

60
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,300
and you turn the other way.
你自己就往另一边转。

61
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,690
That's conservation of angular momentum:
这就是角动量守恒：

62
00:01:54,690 --> 00:01:57,020
the total spin never just disappears.
总的转动，不会凭空消失。

63
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:57,890
When the wheels fail,
轮子一坏，

64
00:01:57,890 --> 00:01:59,760
you're the chair that won't stop spinning.
你就是那把停不下来的转椅。

65
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:02,350
It fired its thrusters to stop the spin. No luck,
它用推进器想刹住，没刹住，

66
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:04,410
and the radio link kept dropping out.
通信也断断续续。

67
00:02:04,410 --> 00:02:06,990
It got within about twelve to fifteen kilometers.
它离Swift最近只有十几公里，

68
00:02:06,990 --> 00:02:09,050
In August, the rescue was called off.
8月份，救援放弃。

69
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:12,040
On September twenty fifth, LINK itself fell back into the air
9月25号，LINK自己先掉回大气层，

70
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:12,850
and burned up.
烧掉了。

71
00:02:12,850 --> 00:02:15,070
Swift is expected to follow within weeks,
Swift预计几周之内跟着落下，

72
00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:16,760
burning up in the atmosphere.
在大气里烧毁。

73
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:17,200
Its data
它留下的数据，

74
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,700
fed about seven thousand scientific papers.
撑起了大约七千篇论文。

75
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:22,950
Friendly fine print: grabbing a spacecraft never built to be grabbed
友情提示：去抓一个没设计让人抓的航天器，

76
00:02:22,950 --> 00:02:25,850
is, we think, something the whole world is still learning.
在我们看来，全世界都还在学。

77
00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:26,520
Katalyst says
Katalyst说，

78
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,460
the data will help the next rescue.
这次的数据会留给下一次救援。

79
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:31,040
So satellites fall not because space is crowded,
所以卫星往下掉，不是因为太空不空，

80
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:33,640
but because of a whisper of air, plus the Sun.
而是那一丁点空气，再加上太阳。

81
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:34,410
Goodbye, Swift.
再见，Swift。

82
00:02:34,410 --> 00:02:36,980
Built for two years. Worked for twenty two.
设计用两年，干了二十二年。

